    "SipSignalOrigin/SipSignalRead/SipNativeSignalRead share explicitly typed actual initial or established SIP provenance. Initial endpoint permissions and established route permissions remain distinct; these signal readers cannot become RTP grants. The prior outgoing-only origin API is replaced without a compatibility alias.",
    "Schema103 records immutable parent_kind and binds each received source to its actual initial connected call or committed telephone lifetime. Established generation/runtime/call/member/Device/route facts are checked against the confirmed descriptor and actual Connection. An established source cannot borrow initial/native custody or invented endpoint/signing fields.",
    "Operations belong to the logical participant, including when its independent configured route account supplies the current signal credential. A fresh source-owner HTTP credential can inspect status; the route account does not inherit that ownership. Installed replay checks current source rights and both original recipient ceilings without new IO or audience capture.",
    "Runtime SipLeg shares exact physical-controller/incarnation checks in both directions. The moved-call monitor installs a managed source subscription with the actual controller/principal, freezes original observations/native registrations before queuing and uses the existing owned native writer, complete current Store interval and original/current Core audience fence.",
    "Monitoring releases authority readers before waits, keeps the previous100ms policy cadence, and polls the managed input separately. An independently authorized signal direction can retain a connected call when current codec permission denies media. Every RTP packet keeps its own media checks.",
    "The generated HTTP reference and developer guide describe both source lifetimes and logical ownership. Frozen wire/result schemas are unchanged."
  ],
